# Workers Assets' headers on the static files
# (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/):
# `just assets` copies this file into worker-assets/.
# Rules here don't apply to the Worker's own responses, which carry the same
# headers from security_headers in crates/server/src/lib.rs.
#
# Every file: no sniffing, the origin only as referrer. The web app's shell
# may be framed only as the projector (/s/) and the verification page (/v/):
# later rules add to earlier ones, and the first rule denies framing
# everywhere, so the two frameable paths can't be matched by it; they are
# listed as the exception instead.
#
# The participant's assets are named by their hash (apps/participant),
# so phones keep them for good; its fallback keeps a fixed name, so phones
# revalidate it, which Assets does by default (max-age=0, must-revalidate,
# with an ETag): this says so.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

/s/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  ! X-Frame-Options

/v/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  ! X-Frame-Options

/participant/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/participant/fallback.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
